# Test fixtures are byte-exact inputs to encoding and content assertions. Git's
# default `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows would convert their LF endings to
# CRLF on checkout, corrupting the encoding fixtures (Big5/GBK/EUC-KR/Shift_JIS
# /Windows-1252 raw bytes, plus their expected decoded forms) and breaking 10
# tests in `crates/tests/core/encoding_matrix.rs` with `actual: "...\r\n"` vs
# `expected: "...\n"`. Marking the whole tree as `binary` tells git to never
# touch line endings, so the working copy matches the object store on every
# platform. The path moved from `tests/fixtures/` to `crates/tests/fixtures/`
# with the test-folder consolidation; this attr must follow.
crates/tests/fixtures/** binary
